  "description": "An F# hardware description language that runs on real FPGAs. One source elaborates a cycle-accurate simulator, a step-through debugger, synthesizable Verilog, and the register-map seam a host driver compiles against — so what you debug is what you deploy. Includes typed ready/valid streams, a numeric layer carrying width, fraction bits and signedness, AXI4-Lite and AXI4 masters, and low-FIRRTL import and export.",
